{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788977434,"nonce":"tVKGFlJLB+vDTczYTTWoFxgRgd4=","message":"Fixed in 048b4ea.\n\ndeclare_native records the unresolvable helper and returns a stub calling\nllvm.trap; promote_function_strict clears the record before lowering and refuses\nthe function if anything landed in it, so the findex stays on the tier below.\nThe record is kept on the stub cache hit too, so a second function reaching the\nsame helper is refused as well. The stub traps rather than being bare\nunreachable because the whole-module path has no such gate.\n\nVerified on the original reproducer: game.hl under --mode jit now prints\n\"[ash] runtime helper hlp_alloc_obj_sized unresolved (...); refusing to compile\ncallers\" and reaches Main.init(), where before it printed repeated\n'beadie-promoter-1' panics.\n\nASH_TEST_UNRESOLVED_NATIVE forces the condition without staging an old runtime;\ncrates/ash_cli/tests/unresolved_helper.rs asserts no thread panics, a clean exit,\nan unchanged answer and that the refusal names the helper.\n\nPoint 2 of this issue -- build.rs silently falling back to the debug cdylib in a\nrelease build -- is NOT addressed here and needs its own change.","files":null}]}